            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Charlie's Mom"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is GREAT!! Of course I had to mess around with it, so I added 1/4 cup red wine vinegar and a little sugar...and a lot more garlic. This basic easy recipe is FANTASTIC, thanks for sharing."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MY4KIDS"
            },
            "reviewBody": "After taking another reviewers suggestion to add 1/4 cup of red wine vinegar and a 1 tsp of sugar, it tasted just like the $4 bottle of Beano's sub oil that you buy at the deli.",
            "datePublished": "2020-05-03T12:21:25.090Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Frank"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Being of Italian decent, I added \"some\" balsamic vinegar, minced the garlic, \"some\" sea salt and black pepper, and added less than 1/4 tsp of onion powder. Then I used a hand plunge blender to emulusfy it. It didn't separate very much and hardly coagulted at 40°f in the refrigerator. I did use the original recipe, first, but felt it needed some change second time around. But the original was good also.",
            "datePublished": "2024-10-05T01:24:00.283Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Angela Cavaletto"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was really good! I did use 1/4 teaspoon of garlic powder instead of the fresh garlic. This is a great substitute for my favorite sub dressing.",
            "datePublished": "2020-08-13T21:21:03.310Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Baking Nana"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this for Faceless Frenzy July 2012 - it had been in my recipe box for a long time - over all this is very tasty but it also needs some red wine vinegar. This would also make a tasty dipping oil for some crusty bread.",
            "datePublished": "2012-07-01T07:03:29.833Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Erica R"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great! But not what Johnny Carino's serves (I used to work there). They just add baked minced garlic to extra virgin olive oil. This is better than that for a sandwich spread!",
            "datePublished": "2007-06-13T16:11:23.137Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
